# Jotan

## Lore

The Jotan, the Earth Giants, are the strongest giants of the Palladium World and its best giant smiths: their weapons and armor are bettered only by Dwarven work and stand level with the Kobolds''. They are not quick-witted and do not mind hard labor, working as soldiers, miners, builders and armorers, and much of what the Cyclops and Nimro carry was made at a Jotan forge.

Few in number, they keep to themselves, but they are fierce toward any smaller folk they meet, and Jotan warlords at the head of goblin, orc, ogre and troll armies have done more than anyone to give giants their name. In the Baalgor Wastelands they are the giants'' enforcers and blacksmiths, with more orders than they can fill and plenty of Gromek to fight.

**Alignment:** Any, but leans toward anarchist and evil.

**Physical Appearance:** Bronze-skinned and powerfully built, with dark eyes and brown hair.

**Size:** 18 to 20 feet tall (5.4 to 6.1 m).

**Average Life Span:** 300 years; some live to 500.

**Habitat:** Anywhere, but mostly the Baalgor Wastelands, the Old Kingdom and the Land of the South Winds.

**Enemies:** Rahu-Men, Titans, Elves, Dwarves and humans by tradition.

**Allies:** Nimro, Cyclops and Gigantes, and trolls, ogres, orcs and goblins. May deal with supernatural beings, creatures of magic and evil sorcerers.

**Favorite Weapons:** Giant-sized large swords, battle axes, ball and chain and blunt weapons, with chain, scale and plate armor.

## GM Notes

A Jotan''s raids on human settlements are frowned on by the other Baalgor giants, who know what provoking humans costs; a Jotan player character with that habit is at odds with its own side. They are often found commanding orcs, goblins and other monster races, and are openly hostile to most non-giants.
